  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">P4R Programme Travel and L&amp;D Allocation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This allocation supports the effective delivery of a regional programme focused on strengthening resilience in Eastern Europe and the South Caucasus. It enables essential travel and learning activities for programme staff to ensure high-quality design, oversight and delivery of development interventions across multiple countries and complex operating environments.
Funding will support in-country engagement with partners, government institutions, civil society organisations and multilateral actors, helping staff to better understand local contexts, assess risks, monitor progress and identify opportunities for positive change. Learning and development activities will strengthen staff skills in areas such as programme management, inclusion, safeguarding, monitoring and learning, and value for money, ensuring that development assistance is delivered responsibly and effectively.
By investing in staff capability and informed engagement, this allocation contributes to stronger institutions, more inclusive public services and improved development outcomes. The activities supported are directly linked to poverty reduction, inclusive growth and long-term stability, in line with the core objectives of Official Development Assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
